<title>RUSSIA: Rouble firm as funds needed for T-bill buying.</title>
<headline>Rouble firm as funds needed for T-bill buying.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The rouble was firm in lively trading on Monday as banks sought funds for investing in government securities, dealers said.</p>
<p> roubles/dollar	Apr 7 midday   Apr 7 early    Apr 4 close</p>
<p> today settlement    5,736-37	 5,734-36	 5,738-40</p>
<p> tomorrow settlement 5,737-38	 5,737-39	 5,735-37</p>
<p> overnight credit (%)   30-35	    20-25	    15-25</p>
<p>			   Apr 7				 Apr 4</p>
<p> central bank	  5,732/46			    5,730/44</p>
<p> MICEX		   5,739				 5,739</p>
<p>&quot;As usual banks are seeking roubles to buy T-bills, at (Wednesday's) auctions as well,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>On April 9 the Russian Finance Ministry will auction six trillion roubles in 364-day Treasury bills (series 23004) and four trillion roubles of an additional tranche of 119-day T-bills (series 22073).</p>
<p>&quot;The T-bill market remains the major trend factor for the rouble/dollar market,&quot; Avtobank dealer Sergei Gornev said.</p>
<p>--Artyom Danielyan, Moscow newsroom (095) 941 8520</p>
